 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [D-NeRF](8660-d-nerf.md)
-D-NeRF synthesizes novel views at arbitrary time instances for dynamic scenes with complex non-rigid geometries, optimizing a deformable volumetric function from a sparse set of monocular input images. It sets itself apart from naive time-extended NeRFs by decomposing the representation into a static canonical space and a learned deformation field, thereby exploiting temporal redundancy that direct 6D mappings fail to capture. Unlike [DaReNeRF](13782-darenerf.md), which focuses on specific deformation regularizations, D-NeRF establishes the foundational canonical-space paradigm for dynamic neural rendering.
